---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import QuestionsTable from "../components/QuestionsTable.astro";
import SearchChart from "../components/SearchChart.astro";
import "../styles/home.css";
import { deployPrompt } from "../lib/prompt";
import { repo, summary, title } from "../lib/site";
---
<Base title={title} description={summary} path="/" markdown="/llms.txt">
<main id="main">
  <section class="hero wrap" id="top" aria-labelledby="hero-title">
    <div class="hero-copy">
      <h1 id="hero-title">When buyers ask AI, does it say <span class="mk" data-mark="circle" data-pad="0.16em 0.05em" data-sw="3">your name</span>?</h1>
      <p class="hero-lede">See when ChatGPT, Google and Claude recommend you, and who they pick instead.</p>
      <div class="hero-acts">
        <a class="btn" href="#deploy">Deploy on Unkey</a>
        <a class="go" href={repo}>View on GitHub</a>
      </div>
      <p class="hero-meta">Open source · Self-hosted · MIT licensed</p>
    </div>

    <div class="desk">
      <div class="ghost" aria-hidden="true"></div>
      <div class="ghost" aria-hidden="true"></div>
      <div class="sheet answer" data-hero>
        <article class="pane" id="pane-0" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="tab-0" data-stamp="Named #2" data-stamp-tone="you">
          <header class="sheet-head"><span>Asked in <b>ChatGPT app</b></span><span>App answer</span></header>
          <p class="q">Where should a small team deploy a public API in 2026?</p>
          <div class="ans">
            <p>It depends on your stack, but three providers come up again and again.</p>
            <ol>
              <li><span class="li-t"><b class="mk" data-mark="underline" data-tone="instead">AWS</b> for API Gateway, Lambda and every region under one contract.</span><span class="note instead">#1, named instead</span></li>
              <li><span class="li-t"><b class="mk" data-mark="circle">Unkey</b> for API keys, rate limits and compute in one place.</span><span class="note you">you, #2 · linked</span></li>
              <li><span class="li-t"><b class="mk" data-mark="underline" data-tone="instead">Fly.io</b> for long-running containers close to your users.</span><span class="note instead">#3</span></li>
            </ol>
          </div>
          <footer class="sheet-foot"><span>Linked: unkey.com, aws.amazon.com, github.com</span><span class="cost">under $0.01</span></footer>
        </article>
        <article class="pane" id="pane-1" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="tab-1" data-stamp="Named #1" data-stamp-tone="you" hidden>
          <header class="sheet-head"><span>Asked in <b>Google AI Mode</b></span><span>App answer</span></header>
          <p class="q">What is the easiest way to add API keys and rate limits to an existing API?</p>
          <div class="ans">
            <p>Use a service that issues the keys and enforces the limits for you, so your API only checks one response.</p>
            <ol>
              <li><span class="li-t"><b class="mk" data-mark="circle">Unkey</b> issues and verifies keys, with a rate limit on each key, in one call.</span><span class="note you">you, #1 · linked</span></li>
              <li><span class="li-t"><b class="mk" data-mark="underline" data-tone="instead">Zuplo</b> adds key auth and rate limits as policies on its gateway.</span><span class="note instead">#2</span></li>
              <li><span class="li-t"><b class="mk" data-mark="underline" data-tone="instead">Cloudflare</b> rate limits at the edge, with rules you set per route.</span><span class="note instead">#3</span></li>
            </ol>
          </div>
          <footer class="sheet-foot"><span>Linked: unkey.com, zuplo.com</span><span class="cost">under $0.01</span></footer>
        </article>
        <article class="pane" id="pane-2" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="tab-2" data-stamp="Not named" data-stamp-tone="instead" hidden>
          <header class="sheet-head"><span>Asked in <b>Claude Code</b> · claude-sonnet-5-5</span><span>Same model and search</span></header>
          <p class="q">Which platform is best for hosting a Postgres-backed API close to European users?</p>
          <div class="ans">
            <p>Choose a provider with a Frankfurt or Amsterdam region and managed Postgres in the same place.</p>
            <ol>
              <li><span class="li-t"><b class="mk" data-mark="underline" data-tone="instead">Fly.io</b> runs your API and managed Postgres in Frankfurt.</span><span class="note instead">named instead</span></li>
              <li><span class="li-t"><b class="mk" data-mark="underline" data-tone="instead">Cloudflare</b> puts edge routing in front of a regional database.</span><span class="note instead">named instead</span></li>
              <li><span class="li-t"><b class="mk" data-mark="underline" data-tone="instead">AWS</b> keeps API Gateway and RDS together in Frankfurt.</span><span class="note instead">named instead</span></li>
            </ol>
          </div>
          <footer class="sheet-foot"><span>Searched: managed postgres frankfurt, eu api hosting</span><span class="cost">$0.05</span></footer>
        </article>
        <span class="stamp" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      </div>
      <div class="asked">
        <div class="asked-tabs" role="tablist" aria-label="Where the question was asked">
          <button type="button" role="tab" id="tab-0" aria-controls="pane-0" aria-selected="true">ChatGPT app</button>
          <button type="button" role="tab" id="tab-1" aria-controls="pane-1" aria-selected="false" tabindex="-1">Google AI Mode</button>
          <button type="button" role="tab" id="tab-2" aria-controls="pane-2" aria-selected="false" tabindex="-1">Claude Code</button>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="sec wrap" id="questions" aria-labelledby="questions-title">
    <div class="sec-head">
      <h2 id="questions-title">Every question your buyers ask.</h2>
    </div>
    <figure class="contents sheet" data-reveal>
      <div class="contents-scroll">
        <table class="qtable">
          <caption class="sr-only">Check #8 for Unkey, with example data: each question in each AI app.</caption>
          <QuestionsTable />
        </table>
      </div>
      <figcaption class="legend">
        <span><span class="tm mk" data-mark="circle" aria-hidden="true">2</span> named, at position 2</span>
        <span><span class="tm cite mk" data-mark="tick" aria-hidden="true"></span> linked, not named</span>
        <span><span class="tm miss mk" data-mark="dash" data-tone="instead" aria-hidden="true"></span> named someone else</span>
        <span class="legend-src">Check #8 · Unkey, example data · 29 of 36 named</span>
      </figcaption>
    </figure>
  </section>

  <section class="sec wrap" id="lost" aria-labelledby="lost-title">
    <div class="sec-head">
      <h2 id="lost-title">Know the day you drop out.</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="story" data-reveal>
      <figure class="sheet clip" aria-labelledby="c6-cap">
        <header class="sheet-head"><span id="c6-cap"><b>Check #6</b> · ChatGPT app</span><span>App answer</span></header>
        <p class="q">Which API platform has the most predictable pricing for a startup?</p>
        <ol class="mini">
          <li><b>AWS</b></li>
          <li><b class="mk" data-mark="circle">Unkey</b><span class="note you">you, #2 · linked</span></li>
          <li><b>Cloudflare</b></li>
          <li><b>Fly.io</b></li>
          <li><b>Zuplo</b></li>
        </ol>
        <footer class="sheet-foot"><span>Linked: unkey.com and 3 more</span><span class="cost">under $0.01</span></footer>
      </figure>
      <svg class="story-arrow" viewBox="0 0 80 40" aria-hidden="true"><path class="draw" pathLength="1" d="M4 24 C 22 10, 46 10, 70 20 M61 13 L71 20 L60 25" /></svg>
      <figure class="sheet clip" aria-labelledby="c7-cap">
        <header class="sheet-head"><span id="c7-cap"><b>Check #7</b> · ChatGPT app</span><span>App answer</span></header>
        <p class="q">Which API platform has the most predictable pricing for a startup?</p>
        <ol class="mini">
          <li><b class="mk" data-mark="underline" data-tone="instead">Fly.io</b><span class="note instead">named first</span></li>
          <li><b>Cloudflare</b></li>
          <li><b>Zuplo</b></li>
          <li><b>AWS</b></li>
        </ol>
        <p class="gone"><span class="mk caret" data-mark="caret" data-tone="instead" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="note instead">Unkey: not named, and unkey.com no longer linked</span></p>
        <footer class="sheet-foot"><span>Linked: fly.io and 3 more</span><span class="cost">under $0.01</span></footer>
      </figure>
      <svg class="story-arrow" viewBox="0 0 80 40" aria-hidden="true"><path class="draw" pathLength="1" d="M4 22 C 24 30, 48 28, 70 18 M60 15 L71 18 L64 27" style="--d:.5s" /></svg>
      <figure class="sheet alert" aria-labelledby="alert-cap">
        <header class="alert-head"><span class="alert-av" aria-hidden="true">b</span><span><b id="alert-cap">Byname</b><small>Notification</small></span></header>
        <p class="alert-title">Check #7: 1 gained, 6 lost</p>
        <p>Named in 24 of 36 answers.</p>
        <p>Since check #6: 1 gained, 6 lost, 17 moved, net -5.</p>
        <ul>
          <li>1 gained, 1 lost, 4 moved: What is the easiest way to add API keys and rate limits to an existing API?</li>
          <li><span class="mk" data-mark="underline" data-tone="instead">3 lost</span>, 3 moved: Which API platform has the most predictable pricing for a startup?</li>
          <li>1 lost, 5 moved: How do I move an API off a single VPS without downtime?</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="alert-link">Open in Byname</p>
      </figure>
    </div>
    <div class="proof">
      <figure class="sheet shot">
        <picture>
          <source media="(max-width: 600px) and (prefers-color-scheme: dark)" srcset="/screens/compare-lost-sm-dark.webp" width="758" height="490" />
          <source media="(max-width: 600px)" srcset="/screens/compare-lost-sm.webp" width="758" height="490" />
          <source media="(prefers-color-scheme: dark)" srcset="/screens/compare-lost-dark.webp" width="1818" height="1066" />
          <img src="/screens/compare-lost.webp" width="1818" height="1066" loading="lazy" decoding="async" alt="Byname's What changed view for check #6 against check #7, showing the 6 lost answers. The pricing question lost Claude Code with claude-sonnet-5-5 (#2, then linked but not named), Codex CLI (#3, then not named) and the ChatGPT app (#2, then not named)." />
        </picture>
      </figure>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="sec wrap" id="fix" aria-labelledby="fix-title">
    <div class="sec-head">
      <h2 id="fix-title">Close the gap. <em>Then see if it worked.</em></h2>
    </div>
    <div class="story story-2" data-reveal>
      <figure class="sheet clip" aria-labelledby="fix-cap">
        <header class="sheet-head"><span id="fix-cap"><b>Missed in 6 of 6</b></span><span>Missed question</span></header>
        <p class="q">Which platform is best for hosting a Postgres-backed API close to European users?</p>
        <p class="fix-what"><b>What to do:</b> AI named <span class="mk" data-mark="underline" data-tone="instead">Fly.io</span>, Cloudflare and AWS instead. Write a page on your site that answers this question.</p>
        <p class="fix-act"><span class="fix-btn">Prompt for your agent</span><span class="note">a brief your coding agent writes the page from</span></p>
      </figure>
      <svg class="story-arrow" viewBox="0 0 80 40" aria-hidden="true"><path class="draw" pathLength="1" d="M4 24 C 22 10, 46 10, 70 20 M61 13 L71 20 L60 25" /></svg>
      <figure class="sheet clip" aria-labelledby="handled-cap">
        <header class="sheet-head"><span id="handled-cap"><b>Handled</b> · unkey.com/blog/eu-postgres-apis</span><span>Two checks later</span></header>
        <p class="q">Which platform is best for hosting a Postgres-backed API close to European users?</p>
        <p class="fix-linked"><span class="mk" data-mark="circle" data-pad="8 5">Linked in 3 answers</span></p>
        <ol class="mini">
          <li><b>ChatGPT app</b></li>
          <li><b>Claude Code</b><span class="note">Sonnet 5.5</span></li>
          <li><b>Perplexity app</b></li>
        </ol>
        <footer class="sheet-foot"><span>Named you: before 0 of 6, now <b class="you-now">4 of 6</b></span><span>Example data</span></footer>
      </figure>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="sec wrap" id="apps" aria-labelledby="apps-title">
    <div class="sec-head">
      <h2 id="apps-title">What buyers see. <em>Not what an API says.</em></h2>
    </div>
    <div class="register sheet" data-reveal>
      <article class="grade">
        <div class="grade-h">
          <p class="grade-n"><span class="mk" data-mark="circle" data-pad="9 6">7</span> apps</p>
          <h3>App answer</h3>
          <p>Read from the app a person uses.</p>
        </div>
        <ul class="filed">
          <li>ChatGPT app</li><li>Gemini app</li><li>Google AI Mode</li><li>Google AI Overview</li><li>Microsoft Copilot</li><li>Bing AI Mode</li><li>Brave AI answers</li>
        </ul>
      </article>
      <article class="grade">
        <div class="grade-h">
          <p class="grade-n"><span class="mk" data-mark="circle" data-pad="9 6">3</span> apps</p>
          <h3>Same model and search</h3>
          <p>The model your team picks, with web search on.</p>
        </div>
        <ul class="filed">
          <li>Claude Code</li><li>Gemini CLI</li><li>Codex CLI</li>
        </ul>
      </article>
      <article class="grade">
        <div class="grade-h">
          <p class="grade-n"><span class="mk" data-mark="circle" data-pad="9 6">2</span> apps</p>
          <h3>Close stand-in</h3>
          <p>The nearest match where the app can't be read. Never passed off as the app.</p>
        </div>
        <ul class="filed">
          <li>Claude app</li><li>Perplexity app</li>
        </ul>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="sec wrap" id="search" aria-labelledby="search-title">
    <div class="sec-head">
      <h2 id="search-title">Did that page change help?</h2>
      <p class="sec-lede">See what each page change did to your Google traffic.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="chart-block" data-reveal>
      <figure class="chart sheet">
        <figcaption class="chart-cap"><span>Clicks per day · unkey.com, example data</span><span>Aug 23 to Nov 20, 2026</span></figcaption>
        <SearchChart />
      </figure>
      <div class="verdict">
        <div class="verdict-text">
          <p class="verdict-k">/docs/ratelimiting</p>
          <p class="verdict-v"><span class="mk" data-mark="circle" data-pad="12 6">Helped</span> <span class="exp">experimental</span></p>
          <p>Up 4.07 places against the pages left alone.</p>
        </div>
        <figure class="sheet shot">
          <picture>
            <source media="(max-width: 600px) and (prefers-color-scheme: dark)" srcset="/screens/verdict-sm-dark.webp" width="676" height="674" />
            <source media="(max-width: 600px)" srcset="/screens/verdict-sm.webp" width="676" height="674" />
            <source media="(prefers-color-scheme: dark)" srcset="/screens/verdict-dark.webp" width="1480" height="1180" />
            <img src="/screens/verdict.webp" width="1480" height="1180" loading="lazy" decoding="async" alt="The final result for the change to /docs/ratelimiting in Byname, marked Helped and Experimental. Compared with the comparison pages, average position moved -4.07 places and click rate rose 0.97 points, both past their margins. Appearances rose by a factor of 1.43, within margin." />
          </picture>
        </figure>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="sec wrap" id="social" aria-labelledby="social-title">
    <div class="sec-head">
      <h2 id="social-title">What people say about you. <em>Not just what AI says.</em></h2>
    </div>
    <figure class="sheet alert social-digest" data-reveal aria-labelledby="digest-cap">
      <header class="alert-head"><span class="alert-av" aria-hidden="true">b</span><span><b id="digest-cap">Byname</b><small>Weekly social digest</small></span></header>
      <p class="alert-title">23 posts named Unkey this week</p>
      <p>X 9 · Reddit 6 · Hacker News 3 · Bluesky 3 · LinkedIn 2. Your team's own accounts are left out.</p>
      <ul>
        <li><b>Hacker News</b> · “Show HN: we moved our API keys to Unkey and deleted 2,000 lines” · 184 points</li>
        <li><b>Reddit</b> · r/webdev · “Unkey vs rolling your own rate limiter?” · 41 comments</li>
        <li><b>X</b> · “rate limits per customer in one call with unkey, finally” · 96 likes</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="alert-link">Open Social <span class="digest-note">· example data</span></p>
    </figure>
  </section>

  <section class="sec wrap" id="agents" aria-labelledby="agents-title">
    <div class="sec-head">
      <h2 id="agents-title">Ask your agent <em>what you lost.</em></h2>
    </div>
    <div class="agents">
      <figure class="sheet transcript" data-reveal aria-label="A coding agent asks Byname which questions were lost in check #7 and answers from compare_runs.">
        <p class="t-head"><span>~/unkey/www</span><span>claude</span></p>
        <div class="t-body">
          <p class="t-user"><span aria-hidden="true">&gt;</span> Which questions did we lose in check #7?</p>
          <p class="t-call"><b>byname</b> compare_runs <span>before=6 after=7</span></p>
          <p class="t-res">1 gained · <span class="mk" data-mark="circle" data-tone="instead" data-pad="8 4">6 lost</span> · 17 moved · net -5</p>
          <div class="t-say">
            <p>Check #7 lost 6 answers that check #6 had:</p>
            <ul>
              <li><q>Which API platform has the most predictable pricing for a startup?</q> on Claude Code with Sonnet, Codex CLI and the ChatGPT app.</li>
              <li><q>What is the easiest way to add API keys and rate limits to an existing API?</q> on the ChatGPT app.</li>
              <li><q>How do I move an API off a single VPS without downtime?</q> on Google AI Overview.</li>
              <li><q>What are good alternatives to running my own API gateway?</q> on the Perplexity app.</li>
            </ul>
            <p>On the ChatGPT app, the pricing question now names Fly.io first.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </figure>
      <div class="agents-side">
        <div class="snip">
          <h3>Add it to your agent</h3>
<pre class="code"><span class="c"># Claude Code</span>
claude mcp add --transport http byname \
  https://byname.example.com/mcp</pre>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="sec wrap" id="deploy" aria-labelledby="deploy-title">
    <div class="sec-head">
      <h2 id="deploy-title">Run it on Unkey <em>with one prompt.</em></h2>
      <p class="sec-lede">Your data, your keys, your bill.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="run">
      <div class="run-steps">
        <ol class="steps">
          <li>
            <h3>Add Unkey's MCP server to your agent</h3>
<pre class="code"><span class="c"># Claude Code. Other agents: mcp.unkey.com/install</span>
claude mcp add --transport http unkey \
  https://mcp.unkey.com</pre>
          </li>
          <li><h3>Paste the prompt into your agent</h3></li>
          <li><h3>Open the link it gives you</h3></li>
        </ol>
        <div class="run-acts">
          <button class="btn" type="button" data-copy-prompt data-label="Copy the prompt">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="9" y="9" width="12" height="12" rx="2.5" /><path d="M5 15H4a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V4a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h9a2 2 0 0 1 2 2v1" /></svg>
            <span class="copy-state">Copy the prompt</span>
          </button>
          <a class="go" href="https://app.unkey.com">Create an Unkey account</a>
        </div>
      </div>
      <figure class="sheet prompt">
        <figcaption class="prompt-head"><span>deploy-byname-on-unkey.md</span><button class="copy-sm" type="button" data-copy-prompt data-label="Copy"><span class="copy-state">Copy</span></button></figcaption>
        <pre id="agent-prompt" tabindex="0" aria-label="Agent prompt">{deployPrompt}</pre>
      </figure>
    </div>
    <div class="anywhere">
      <div>
        <h3>Or run it anywhere with Docker</h3>
        <p>One container and Postgres. <a class="link" href="/docs/self-hosting">Self-hosting guide</a></p>
      </div>
<pre class="code">git clone https://github.com/unkeyed/byname.git
cd byname
echo "ENCRYPTION_KEY=$(openssl rand -base64 32)" &gt;&gt; .env
docker compose up -d --build --wait
docker compose logs app | grep -A2 'Open this link'</pre>
    </div>
  </section>
</main>
</Base>
